From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: add the SLPI FastRPC remote heap

The Pocket 5 IMU is an ICM-4x6xx behind the SLPI sensor core, not an
ADSP static PD. That PD asks the host for a remote heap when it attaches
and does not start without one. Assign the heap to SSC_Q6 (VMID 5), which
is the VM the SLPI sensor firmware expects. The FastRPC driver only
hands the region over when a static PD attaches, so a board whose SLPI
never starts leaves it an idle, reusable pool.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -863,6 +863,15 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x8bf00000 0x0 0x4600000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/* Remote heap for the SLPI sensors PD; reusable while idle */
+		slpi_rpc_remote_heap_mem: slpi-rpc-remote-heap {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
+			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
+			size = <0x0 0xc00000>;
+			reusable;
+		};
 	};
 
 	smem {
@@ -3121,6 +3130,9 @@
 					compatible = "qcom,fastrpc";
 					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
 					label = "sdsp";
+					memory-region = <&slpi_rpc_remote_heap_mem>;
+					/* SSC_Q6 */
+					qcom,vmids = <0x5>;
 					qcom,non-secure-domain;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
 					#size-cells = <0>;
